course: dictionary
lesson: 15982
title: Upriver: against the flow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Upriver means towards the source of a river, which is where the river starts. You go against the flow of the water, like climbing back up a slide. «The canoe paddled upriver, fighting the strong current.» The canoeists were heading towards the source, against the water.
explain: Upriver can also mean at a place further up the river from where you are. «The fishing hut is two miles upriver.» Stand where you are, look towards the source, and the hut is that way.
explain: The opposite is downriver, which means towards the mouth, where the river reaches the sea or a lake. Upstream is close in meaning to upriver. When you meet upriver, ask: is the writer talking about the source, or about a place further up from me?
fact: Upriver means towards the source of a river, against the flow of the water.
fact: «Upriver» also means at a place further up the river from where you are.
fact: Rivers flow from the source to the mouth, so going upriver is often going uphill.
fact: «Upstream» is close in meaning to upriver, and «downriver» is its opposite.
fact: Salmon swim upriver to lay their eggs.
exercise: «The explorers paddled upriver for three days.» What does upriver mean here? | Along the riverbank on dry land | *Towards the source of the river, against the flow | Across the river from bank to bank | Down to the mouth, where the river meets the sea
exercise: Which word is the opposite of upriver? | Sideways | *Downriver | Across | Upstream
exercise: «The salmon swam upriver to lay their eggs.» Where were the salmon going? | Into a still lake | Out to sea, with the water | *Towards the river's source, against the water | Round and round in circles
test: «The fishing hut is two miles upriver from the bridge.» Where is the hut? | On the bridge itself | Further down the river from the bridge | Under the water | *Further up the river from the bridge
test: Kwame and his dad paddled against the current all morning. Which way did they go? | Across the lake | Downriver, towards the sea | They stayed still in one place | *Upriver, towards the source
exam: «The boat went upriver against the strong current.» Which words are the clue that upriver means against the flow? | the boat went | *against the strong current | the | upriver
